{%- comment -%}
  When a coming-soon piece goes live: its hikari.release date (Date and time metafield),
  else the Edition day from theme settings. Plain text, for the card and the product page.
  The format is date_formats.release in each locale file. It is read as text and passed to date
  as a pattern, because date: format: '…' prints the time in UTC, not the shop's time zone.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign rel = p.metafields.hikari.release.value -%}
{%- assign rel_format = 'date_formats.release' | t -%}
{%- if rel -%}{{ rel | date: rel_format }}{%- else -%}{{ settings.edition_day }}{%- endif -%}
